  "test_scope": [
    "Two real Android camera-permission denial dialogs; camera hardware is never opened.",
    "Cancellation directly tests the OS empty-callback protocol, not a physical dialog dismissal.",
    "New-process denial history, OS grant, durable denial clearing and new-process revocation.",
    "Typed Rust permission observations/events and seven special-access status queries.",
    "Actual virtual SetText/UTF16 selection/Unicode movement/copy/cut/paste/clear-focus routing.",
    "Isolated virtual-tree tests cover hidden nodes, subtree search, secret value withholding, cycles, focused-node hiding and unsupported actions."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Physical TalkBack speech/gestures, Switch Access, real autofill-provider compatibility and OEM/API matrix are not certified by these emulator checks.",
    "Permission settingsRequired is inferred from a completed denial plus no rationale; public APIs cannot prove every admin/policy/auto-reset state.",
    "Special-access status is tested; granting each special access through every OEM settings UI is not claimed.",
    "Visual wrapped-line movement is not advertised without layout line metadata; custom drawn views must describe their semantics.",
    "Generic permission support does not supply every corresponding Android sensor/SDK implementation or establish complete Flutter parity."
  ]
